{{Quote|Our target is this Cyber Center. It's the 'brains' of the entire Separatist campaign here on Anaxes.|Clone Commander CC-2224 "Cody"|<ref name="The Bad Batch" />}}
The '''Cyber Center''' was a structure on the [[planet]] [[Anaxes]] utilized by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] during the [[Battle of Anaxes]]. The center was used during the course of the battle by Separatist [[Admiral]] [[Trench]], to receive an [[Rex's battle strategy algorithm|algorithm]] from [[Skako Minor]] which he used to predict the [[Galactic Republic]]'s tactics.

==History==
As the [[Clone Wars]] raged on throughout [[the galaxy]], it eventually came to the [[planet]] [[Anaxes]], home to a crucial [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] [[Anaxes shipyards|shipyard facility]]. To gain a tactical advantage in the battle, [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] [[Admiral]] [[Trench]] utilized a stolen [[Rex's battle strategy algorithm|strategy algorithm]] obtained from [[Advanced Recon Commando|ARC trooper]] CT-1409 "[[Echo]]," who was in [[Techno Union]] custody in their headquarters on [[Skako Minor]] after he was believed by the Republic to have [[Death|perished]] during the [[Battle of Lola Sayu]].<ref name="The Bad Batch" /> The algorithm would be sent to the Cyber Center on the planet's surface, which Trench could access at any time from his Separatist dreadnought, the ''[[Invulnerable]]''.<ref name="Unfinished Business">{{TCW|Unfinished Business (episode)}}</ref>

[[File:OOM_Droid_Trench_Anaxes.png|thumb|left|250px|An [[OOM command battle droid]] outside the center.]]
[[Clone Captain]] [[Rex]] believed that the Separatists were combating his personal combat strategy, and, after he and [[Clone Commander]] [[Cody]] received approval from [[Jedi General]] [[Mace Windu]], the two led [[Jesse]], [[Kix]], and [[clone commando]] [[squad]] [[Clone Force 99]] on an operation to infiltrate the Cyber Center. Despite Commander Cody sustaining injuries and being taken back to the Republic base along with Kix, the remaining members pressed on towards the center, eventually coming to and taking a nearby [[Anaxes Separatist Security Outpost|Separatist outpost]]. Fleeing the outpost before Separatist reinforcements arrived, the team positioned themselves around the Cyber Center and infiltrated it just as the reinforcements arrived at the outpost. Within the center, Rex and [[Tech]], a member of Clone Force 99, accessed a [[computer]] and discovered the source of Rex's algorithm, Skako Minor, as well as who was sending it: Echo.<ref name="The Bad Batch" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Cyber Center first appeared in "[[The Bad Batch (episode)|The Bad Batch]]," an episode of ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' that first premiered as an story reel<ref name="Story reel Bad Batch">{{SW|url=video/the-bad-batch-star-wars-the-clone-wars-story-reel|text=Star Wars: The Clone Wars - Story Reel: The Bad Batch|nolive=1}}</ref> in [[2015]]<ref name="Anaheim Announcement">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-clone-wars-bad-batch-4-episode-arc-coming-to-star-wars-celebration|text=''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' "Bad Batch" 4-Episode Arc Coming to ''Star Wars'' Celebration|nolive=1}}</ref> before the finished episode debuted<ref name="The Bad Batch" /> on [[Disney+]] in [[2020]].<ref name="Press Release">{{WebCite|url=https://collider.com/new-on-disney-plus-february-2020|text=What's New on Disney Plus February 2020, Including Toy Story 4|author=Gregory Lawrance|archivedate=20200221195811}}</ref> The subtitles for the episode revealed the Cyber Center's capitalization.<ref name="The Bad Batch" />

